WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
47 years of tracking shows strength falling from age 35, even in regular exercises. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 214. Researchers followed the same people across nearly five decades and measured objective markers of strength and endurance rather than cell reports, according to Science Daily. The rate of loss itself speeds up with advancing age. Adults who began exercising still recorded measurable gains relative to their own baseline. That within-person design supplies rare evidence instead of a

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.200
cross-sectional snapshot.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.820
Routine strength assessments in the 30s

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.640
could flag opportunities for targeted activity adjustments

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:37.980
before losses compound.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.140
One open question is whether resistance volume

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.360
or recovery intervals alter the slope after that inflection.

00:00:45.473 --> 00:00:47.453
Ascension Island went from volcanic rock

00:00:47.453 --> 00:00:50.653
to humid cloud forest after 19th century plantings

00:00:50.653 --> 00:00:52.513
organized by two British scientists.

00:00:53.373 --> 00:00:55.953
Seed plantings drawn from empire botanical gardens,

00:00:56.613 --> 00:00:58.613
documented in historical nautical charts,

00:00:58.613 --> 00:01:03.573
sites, logbooks, and letters, converted a sunscorch site with only a few fern species

00:01:03.573 --> 00:01:07.533
into rainforests within five decades, fizz.org reports.

00:01:08.073 --> 00:01:12.693
Researchers from Pompeo Faber University spent a month on the island collecting historical

00:01:12.693 --> 00:01:16.573
records, ecological data, and soil microbiome samples.

00:01:17.213 --> 00:01:22.893
Victor Mall led the work at the Complex Systems Laboratory under Ricard Soleil, with Nastasia

00:01:22.893 --> 00:01:26.733
notalsator handling post-doctoral contributions on microbiology.

00:01:26.733 --> 00:01:32.013
The team is now building models of the reverse process to test whether other degraded ecosystems

00:01:32.013 --> 00:01:33.073
can be restored.

00:01:33.713 --> 00:01:39.313
Soil microbiome analysis is being completed with the BioFun Lab in Seville to identify rapid

00:01:39.313 --> 00:01:40.593
nutrient-driven changes.

00:01:41.253 --> 00:01:45.873
Sharp transitions from rainforest to desert conditions now appear within a 10-minute walk.

00:01:46.749 --> 00:01:52.029
Commodity microplastics spontaneously produce reactive oxygen species in water, without

00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:55.129
put rising alongside interfacial hydrophobicity.

00:01:55.129 --> 00:02:00.949
Abinitio calculations in nature link the effect to partial salvation and electrostatic forces

00:02:00.949 --> 00:02:04.569
that favor hydroxide oxidation at the plastic water boundary.

00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:09.129
Radical generation scales with surface properties rather than bulk chemistry.

00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:15.009
Hydroxide oxidation becomes energetically more favorable at increasingly hydrophobic interfaces

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:18.289
through combined partial salvation and electrostatic effects.

00:02:18.809 --> 00:02:23.729
The findings indicate direct implications for biomolecular adsorption and cellular damage.

00:02:23.729 --> 00:02:29.056
average. Most people assume everyday plastics sit chemically idle once they reach water or

00:02:29.056 --> 00:02:33.856
living tissue. Spectroscopic measurements and computational modeling instead mapped

00:02:33.856 --> 00:02:39.096
a structure activity relationship at the polymer water boundary itself. The six polymers

00:02:39.096 --> 00:02:45.736
put through that combined test were polyethylene, polypropylene, polystyrene, polyvinyl chloride,

00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:51.516
polymethylmethacrylate, and polyethylene tariff the late. All six turn up in ordinary

00:02:51.516 --> 00:02:57.596
consumer products. Partial salvation of hydroxide ions at these interfaces lowers the energy barrier

00:02:57.596 --> 00:03:03.196
for electron transfer. That drop in the barrier enables hydroxyl radicals to form without any

00:03:03.196 --> 00:03:08.876
external energy input. Microplastics are now detected in human tissues and most ecosystems.

00:03:09.576 --> 00:03:14.656
The surface chemistry identified here offers one mechanistic link between plastic exposure and

00:03:14.656 --> 00:03:20.336
observed cellular stress responses. The same process can promote protein aggregation and membrane

00:03:20.336 --> 00:03:26.156
damage in exposed cells. Those interfacial properties also influence how proteins absorb and

00:03:26.156 --> 00:03:31.896
clump on plastic surfaces. Future material design that reduces surface hydrophobicity or

00:03:31.896 --> 00:03:38.236
alters interfacial charge may lower this unintended reactivity. Changing surface charge or hydrophobicity

00:03:38.236 --> 00:03:43.016
during manufacturing could cut both radical production and downstream biological effects.

00:03:43.676 --> 00:03:47.196
bulk material properties that make plastics useful would stay the same.

00:03:47.196 --> 00:03:52.645
Since an adi children's doctors used a new gene therapy approach that enabled some children

00:03:52.645 --> 00:03:58.705
born deaf to regain hearing, WLWT reports, the treatment targets the underlying genetic

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:01.565
cause rather than providing external amplification.

00:04:02.285 --> 00:04:05.485
Early results show functional improvement in auditory responses.

00:04:06.105 --> 00:04:08.905
The work focuses on restoring natural hearing pathways.

00:04:09.585 --> 00:04:12.745
Patients in the program have specific genetic forms of deafness.

00:04:12.745 --> 00:04:18.741
Find particulate matter from aircraft combustion increases its ability to trigger oxidative stress

00:04:18.741 --> 00:04:20.401
after aging in the atmosphere.

00:04:21.081 --> 00:04:26.041
Laboratory tests described by Fizz.org measured that change in oxidative potential under

00:04:26.041 --> 00:04:27.121
controlled conditions.

00:04:27.481 --> 00:04:30.381
The particles penetrate deep into the respiratory tract.

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:32.801
Once there, they promote inflammation.

00:04:33.441 --> 00:04:38.161
Atmospheric aging therefore alters the harmful properties of these combustion-derived particles

00:04:38.161 --> 00:04:39.461
after they leave the engine.

00:04:39.461 --> 00:04:45.080
McGill University researchers documented that city development reduces the usual increase

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:50.420
in bird species richness toward the tropics. The study compared urban and non-urban sites

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:55.940
across multiple latitudes, according to Fizz.org. The effect narrows the classic biodiversity

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:02.260
pattern observed in natural habitats. Urbanization disrupts one of Earth's most consistent ecological

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:07.813
gradients. Australian producers already have a growing set of practical measures for lowering

00:05:07.813 --> 00:05:13.013
agricultural greenhouse gas output. CSIRO identified those options in a

00:05:13.013 --> 00:05:17.693
report covered by Fizz.org. The analysis also flags additional research

00:05:17.693 --> 00:05:22.233
opportunities for further reductions. The report emphasizes solutions that fit

00:05:22.233 --> 00:05:27.033
existing farm operations. Immediate actions sit alongside longer-term research

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:32.394
needs for emissions cuts across Australian agriculture. The EIT food consumer

00:05:32.394 --> 00:05:36.054
observatory found many people remain curious about precision fermentation

00:05:36.054 --> 00:05:39.394
but needs specific answers before trying them.

00:05:40.034 --> 00:05:42.654
Qualitative research released ahead of World Food Day

00:05:42.654 --> 00:05:46.614
and reported by Fizz.org focused on questions around safety,

00:05:46.974 --> 00:05:48.274
taste, and production methods.

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:52.394
The work examined consumer responses to novel food technologies.

00:05:52.954 --> 00:05:56.354
Clear information gaps currently limit willingness to taste the results.

00:05:57.054 --> 00:06:00.234
Companies that address those points directly may accelerate adoption.

00:06:01.102 --> 00:06:05.402
Before we go, soil microbiome analysis from the ascension island sampling

00:06:05.402 --> 00:06:08.042
is being completed with the Biofun Lab in Seville.

